<!-- Sprint 28d Stage 6 / S3: org.jawata.samples — the CURE SPECIMENS, in the
     upstream pattern repository's own form.

     BUILT, because an address that points at code which does not compile is
     worse than no address, and the cures ship an address.

     NOT SHIPPED: these artifacts are deliberately absent from build/dist, so
     the dist-completeness enforcer keeps the product byte-identical. The
     samples are read on GitHub or in a workspace, never loaded at runtime.

     NO DEPENDENCIES, by design. A specimen that needed the engine to compile
     would couple the product's dependency graph to demonstration code.

     WHY THIS IS AN AGGREGATOR WITH ONE MODULE PER SLUG, and not one module
     with build-helper add-source. The upstream form is <slug>/README.md beside
     <slug>/src/main/java, so two slugs are two source roots, and a Maven
     module carries exactly one <sourceDirectory>. build-helper's add-source
     would compile both from a single module — and it was REJECTED on a
     measurement, not on taste: jawata's project importer does not index
     add-source roots. build/tests-mcp adds src/extra/java that way, and
     search_symbols resolves the class it holds ONLY inside the built jar,
     never as source. Sprint 28d requires every samples-lane address to OPEN in
     the workspace; under add-source the build would go green while
     search_symbols found nothing, which is the failure this stage exists to
     end. One module per slug gives the importer one source root each, and it
     is the upstream layout anyway.

     Adding a specimen therefore means adding a <module> here. That is the
     intended friction: the module list and the slug directories are the same
     fact, and a specimen with no module would not compile and so could not
     silently ship a rotten address. -->
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
    <parent>
        <groupId>org.jawata</groupId>
        <artifactId>org.jawata.build</artifactId>
        <version>3.17.0</version>
    </parent>

    <artifactId>org.jawata.samples</artifactId>
    <packaging>pom</packaging>

    <modules>
        <module>compose-method</module>
        <module>replace-pattern-with-idiom</module>
    </modules>
</project>
